    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="1397" n="1383" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/10–944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Document No. C.60, 6 October, 1944: Letter From the
                        Chairman of the United Nations War Crimes Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurst</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the British Secretary of State for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Eden</hi>)<anchor n="10" xml:id="d887-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-10-06">October 6, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to transmit to you
                    herewith the text of a draft convention which has been prepared by this
                    Commission for the establishment of a United Nations War Crimes Court, together
                    with an explanatory memorandum, (C.50(1) and C.58<anchor n="11" xml:id="d887-f2"
                    />).</p>
                <p>There are also included the text of a recommendation for the establishment of
                    supreme military commanders of mixed Military Tribunals for the trial of War
                    Criminals, together with suggestions to accompany the recommendation (C.52(1)
                    and C.59<anchor n="12" xml:id="d887-f3"/>).</p>
                <pb facs="1398" n="1384" xml:id="pg1384"/>
                <p>In transmitting these documents I am asked to inform you that the Commission
                    unanimously expressed the hope that you would be so good as to take the
                    necessary steps to convene in the near future a diplomatic conference to
                    consider, and if thought fit to conclude, a convention for the establishment of
                    a United Nations War Crimes Court.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil</hi> J. B. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Hurst</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d887-f1" n="10" type="source" xml:id="d887-f1-content">
